WEBVTT

1
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Nathan B.: Morning, all. Let's start with the launch.

2
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Daniel K.: The pricing page is on staging, with both prices and the trial terms.

3
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Nathan B.: Launch readiness. The pricing page is done, the launch email is drafted, and billing has one open case: clinics mid-trial on the old plan.

4
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Emma C.: And Shah's support macros for self-serve signups are ready for launch day.

5
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Anna H.: Billing is the one I'm watching.

6
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Nathan B.: I went back through the list from the 5th.

7
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Nathan B.: Every blocker we raised since 5 October is now closed or owned with a date.

8
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.000
Emma C.: Even the annual question?

9
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Nathan B.: Owned. I decide once legal answers.

10
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.000
Nathan B.: Anna, the mid-trial case.

11
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:14.000
Anna H.: Chidi and I looked at it on Friday.

12
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.000
Anna H.: On billing: we'll handle the mid-trial case in billing by Thursday.

13
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.000
Nathan B.: Thursday is fine.

14
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.000
Emma C.: What do clinics see in the meantime?

15
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:20.000
Emma C.: And the billing FAQ should say what happens mid-trial.

16
00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:32.000
Nathan B.: Agreed, once we know what happens to them.

17
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.000
Daniel K.: Who owns the FAQ these days?

18
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.000
Emma C.: Not sure anymore.

19
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.000
Anna H.: So do mid-trial clinics move to the new price?

20
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.000
Emma C.: Nobody should pay more halfway through a trial.

21
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Nathan B.: Decision: clinics mid-trial keep their old trial terms, and the new pricing applies from their first invoice.

22
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.000
Anna H.: That's simple to build.

23
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.000
Emma C.: And simple to explain.

24
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:43.000
Nathan B.: When does billing stop changing?

25
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.000
Anna H.: We need a freeze before the go/no-go.

26
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:27.000
Anna H.: Then billing changes freeze on 23 October, three days before go/no-go.

27
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.000
Nathan B.: Agreed.

28
00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.000
Daniel K.: Noted for the release notes.

29
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.000
Nathan B.: Anna, the incident follow-ups.

30
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.000
Anna H.: Two updates.

31
00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:28.000
Anna H.: Incident follow-up: the per-clinic rate limits are live. The five-minute alert ships Wednesday.

32
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.000
Nathan B.: Great. Any complaints since?

33
00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.000
Anna H.: None since they went live.

34
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.000
Emma C.: Who runs the go/no-go?

35
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:54.000
Nathan B.: Me, as we agreed on the 14th.

36
00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:16.000
Nathan B.: I'll run the go/no-go Monday morning, everyone brings their checklist.

37
00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.000
Anna H.: What time?

38
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.000
Nathan B.: Nine thirty.

39
00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:22.000
Nathan B.: Last, onboarding.

40
00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:42.000
Emma C.: Daniel has the numbers.

41
00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:08.000
Daniel K.: Onboarding: calendar connects in the email test are at 79% versus 72%.

42
00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:14.000
Nathan B.: Same as last week.

43
00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:30.000
Emma C.: We decide on the full rollout at the end of the month.
